    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the retention, but honestly, a dip in early cohort retention is super common when a product is evolving that fast. It usually just means they're weeding out the \"tourists\" to make room for the power users. \n\nThe pitch deck emphasizes that they're intentionally moving away from mass-market churn toward a high-LTV (lifetime value) model. If you look at the revenue per user in the last few months, it's actually trending up, right? Try to look at the macro picture here. If we're trying to build a thesis for a strong investment, how could we interpret these recent numbers as part of a healthy transition rather than just a failure to retain?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
