      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the revenue per user trend is still up, indicating that the investment thesis of switching to a high-LTV model might actually be playing out. I'd frame this as a sign that the founders are successfully up-skinning their customer base, targeting higher-value users. This pivot is a correctable misstep, and the plateau in MOU numbers might simply be a necessary step towards reaching a more balanced user acquisition and retention pace, ultimately resulting in a healthier business model.",
